<nav class="nav" id="nav" data-screen-label="Nav"><svg class="sunmark" viewBox="0 0 32 32" aria-hidden="true"><circle class="sun-disc" cx="16" cy="16" r="10"></circle></svg><a class="wm" href="/">AMPM <small>BUILDING SERVICES</small></a><div class="links"><a href="/services/" class="">Services</a><a href="/work/" class="">Work</a><a href="/compliance/" class="">Compliance</a><a href="/about/" class="">About</a><a href="/contact/" class="">Contact</a></div><a class="phone" href="tel:03300430080">0330 043 0080</a></nav><div class="page" style="--svc: var(--m-orange);"><div class="shell"><section class="sec p-hero"><div class="reveal in"><span class="svc-bar" style="background: var(--m-orange);"></span></div><div class="reveal in"><div class="kicker">Fabric &amp; Building Envelope</div></div><h1 class="reveal d1 in">Intrusive Fabric Surveys &amp; Compliance</h1><p class="lede reveal d2 in">Intrusive fabric surveys, façade condition surveys and fire-strategy review: the front end that gets the specification right before remediation starts. We open up the external wall, record exactly what is built, close it up properly and hand the assessor the evidence a PAS 9980 appraisal needs. Then we set the specification the works are delivered to.</p><div class="reveal d3 in" style="margin-top: 28px;"><a class="btn line sm" href="/contact/">Enquire about a fabric survey →</a></div></section><section class="sec tight"><div class="reveal in" style="margin-bottom: 32px;"><div class="kicker">What we deliver</div><h2 class="dhead sm">Survey &amp; Compliance,<br>self-delivered.</h2></div><div class="capgroups reveal in"><div class="capgroup"><h4><span class="dot" style="background: var(--m-orange);"></span><span>Scope</span></h4><ul><li>Intrusive fabric surveys (opening up, recording, making good)</li><li>Façade &amp; condition surveys</li><li>Fire-strategy review</li><li>EWS1-related remedial works</li><li>Specification &amp; design coordination</li><li>Records &amp; golden-thread documentation</li></ul></div><div class="capgroup"><h4><span class="dot" style="background: var(--m-orange);"></span><span>Standards &amp; compliance</span></h4><ul><li>Building Safety Act 2022 - higher-risk buildings</li><li>BS 8414 &amp; BR 135 - cladding fire performance</li><li>RICS &amp; relevant survey guidance</li><li>CDM 2015 throughout</li></ul></div></div></section><section class="sec tight"><div class="reveal in" style="margin-bottom: 28px;"><div class="kicker">Intrusive fabric surveys</div><h2 class="dhead sm">Open it up, record it,<br>close it properly.</h2></div><div class="capgroups reveal in"><div class="capgroup"><h4><span class="dot" style="background: var(--m-orange);"></span><span>What an intrusive survey is</span></h4><ul><li>Localised opening-up of the external wall at agreed positions to see the real build-up: outer skin, cavity, insulation, barriers, fixings and substrate</li><li>Needed when drawings are missing, unreliable or contradicted by what is on the wall, which on older and re-clad buildings is most of the time</li><li>The evidence a fire-risk appraisal of external walls (FRAEW) to PAS 9980, an EWS1 assessor or an insurer relies on to judge the wall rather than guess at it</li></ul></div><div class="capgroup"><h4><span class="dot" style="background: var(--m-orange);"></span><span>What we do on site</span></h4><ul><li>Agree the opening-up schedule with the assessor and the building owner: locations, sizes, and what has to be seen at each one</li><li>Open up from access equipment or rope access, photograph and measure every layer, sample where instructed and label everything to the location plan</li><li>Reinstate to a weathertight, fire-compliant condition the same day, with cavity barriers and fixings made good, not left as holes behind a patch</li></ul></div><div class="capgroup"><h4><span class="dot" style="background: var(--m-orange);"></span><span>What you get back</span></h4><ul><li>A photographic record per opening, keyed to elevations, with measured build-ups and a materials schedule</li><li>The record formatted so the assessor can drop it straight into the appraisal, and so it can sit in the golden-thread file for the building</li><li>A costed remediation specification if the appraisal calls for works, delivered by the same team under our <a href="/fabric/bsa-remediation/">building-safety remediation</a> line</li></ul></div></div><p class="body reveal in" style="max-width:70ch;margin:24px 0 0;">A plain boundary: we carry out the opening-up, the recording and the remediation. The fire-risk appraisal itself, and any EWS1 form, is signed by a suitably qualified fire engineer or assessor. We work alongside them, we do not replace them.</p></section><section class="sec tight"><div class="reveal in" style="margin-bottom: 28px;"><div class="kicker">FAQs</div><h2 class="dhead sm">Your questions,<br>answered.</h2></div><div class="faq reveal in"><details class="faq-item"><summary>What is an intrusive fabric survey?</summary><p>An intrusive fabric survey opens up the external wall at agreed points so the actual build-up can be seen and recorded: cladding, cavity, insulation, cavity barriers, fixings and substrate. It is carried out where drawings are missing or cannot be trusted, and it provides the evidence a fire-risk appraisal of external walls (PAS 9980) or an EWS1 assessment relies on. We open up, record, sample where instructed and reinstate to a weathertight, fire-compliant condition.</p></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>Who signs off the fire-risk appraisal?</summary><p>A suitably qualified fire engineer or assessor. We provide the intrusive survey evidence and deliver any remediation the appraisal calls for, but the appraisal and any EWS1 form are theirs to sign. Keeping that boundary clear is part of how the record stands up later.</p></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>What does a façade survey involve?</summary><p>We survey the existing envelope, assess its condition and review the fire strategy - including intrusive investigation where needed - then set a traceable specification before any work starts.</p></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>Do you carry out works related to an EWS1 assessment?</summary><p>We deliver the remedial works that an EWS1 process can identify on the external wall system. The EWS1 form itself is signed by a suitably qualified assessor; we scope, specify and deliver the resulting works.</p></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>Do you produce the records needed for the safety case?</summary><p>Yes. We document the survey, specification and works as golden-thread records, giving you a traceable pack for the building's safety case under the Building Safety Act 2022.</p></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>Which areas do you cover?</summary><p>London and the South East, including Sussex, Surrey, Kent, Hampshire and Berkshire.</p></details></div></section><section class="sec tight"><div class="reveal in" style="margin-bottom: 28px;"><div class="kicker">Part of Fabric &amp; Building Envelope</div><h2 class="dhead sm">Explore the full<br>package.</h2></div><div class="sectorrow reveal in"><a class="sector" href="/fabric/">Fabric &amp; Building Envelope overview</a><a class="sector" href="/fabric/facade-cladding/">Façade &amp; Cladding</a><a class="sector" href="/fabric/roofing/">Roofing</a><a class="sector" href="/fabric/bsa-remediation/">Building-Safety (BSA) Remediation</a></div></section><section class="sec tight line-top xlinks" data-xlink><div class="reveal in" style="margin-bottom: 22px;"><div class="kicker">Explore more</div><h2 class="dhead sm">Related across<br>AMPM Building&nbsp;Services.</h2></div><div class="xgroup reveal in"><span class="xlabel">More in Fabric &amp; Envelope</span><div class="sectorrow"><a class="sector" href="/fabric/">All Fabric &amp; Envelope →</a><a class="sector" href="/fabric/facade-cladding/">Façade &amp; Cladding</a><a class="sector" href="/fabric/roofing/">Roofing</a><a class="sector" href="/fabric/bsa-remediation/">BSA Remediation</a></div></div><div class="xgroup reveal in"><span class="xlabel">Sectors we serve</span><div class="sectorrow"><a class="sector" href="/sectors/residential/">Residential &amp; BTR</a><a class="sector" href="/sectors/healthcare/">Healthcare</a><a class="sector" href="/sectors/education/">Education</a><a class="sector" href="/sectors/">All sectors →</a></div></div><div class="xgroup reveal in"><span class="xlabel">Areas we cover</span><div class="sectorrow"><a class="sector" href="/areas/london/">London</a><a class="sector" href="/areas/crawley-gatwick/">Crawley &amp; Gatwick</a><a class="sector" href="/areas/brighton-hove/">Brighton &amp; Hove</a><a class="sector" href="/areas/guildford-surrey/">Guildford &amp; Surrey</a><a class="sector" href="/areas/west-sussex/">West Sussex</a><a class="sector" href="/areas/east-sussex/">East Sussex</a><a class="sector" href="/areas/surrey/">Surrey</a><a class="sector" href="/areas/kent/">Kent</a><a class="sector" href="/areas/hampshire/">Hampshire</a><a class="sector" href="/areas/berkshire/">Berkshire</a><a class="sector" href="/areas/">All areas &rarr;</a></div></div></section><section class="sec tight line-top"><div class="reveal in" style="margin-bottom: 24px;"><div class="kicker">The other three lines</div><h2 class="dhead sm">One contractor,<br>four service lines.</h2></div><div class="otherlines reveal in"><a class="otherline" href="/commercial/"><span class="ol-l"><span class="ol-sw" style="background: var(--m-purple);"></span><span class="ol-nm">Commercial</span></span><span class="ol-go">→</span></a><a class="otherline" href="/fabric/"><span class="ol-l"><span class="ol-sw" style="background: var(--m-orange);"></span><span class="ol-nm">Fabric</span></span><span class="ol-go">→</span></a><a class="otherline" href="/external-works/"><span class="ol-l"><span class="ol-sw" style="background: var(--m-blue);"></span><span class="ol-nm">External Works</span></span><span class="ol-go">→</span></a></div></section></div><section class="band" data-nav-dark="true" style="background: var(--m-green); color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><div class="shell"><div class="cta-split reveal in"><div><div class="kicker on-dark">Talk to us about MEPH</div><h2 class="dhead sm" style="color: rgb(255, 255, 255);">Scope, programme,<br>stage - send it over.</h2><p class="body" style="color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9); margin-top: 16px;">A named contact, not a sales team, comes back within 24 hours. Include the package, programme and stage if you can.</p></div><div class="cta-row2" style="flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start;"><a class="btn ghost" href="/contact/">Enquire about MEPH →</a><a class="btn ghost" href="/compliance/">Compliance &amp; BSA</a></div></div></div></section></div><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "{{@site.url}}/"}, {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Services", "item": "{{@site.url}}/services/"}, {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "Fabric & Building Envelope", "item": "{{@site.url}}/fabric/"}, {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 4, "name": "Intrusive Fabric Surveys & Compliance", "item": "{{@site.url}}/fabric/survey-compliance/"}]}</script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "What is an intrusive fabric survey?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "An intrusive fabric survey opens up the external wall at agreed points so the actual build-up can be seen and recorded: cladding, cavity, insulation, cavity barriers, fixings and substrate. It is carried out where drawings are missing or cannot be trusted, and it provides the evidence a fire-risk appraisal of external walls (PAS 9980) or an EWS1 assessment relies on. We open up, record, sample